# Anchored to the repo root. Unanchored `data/` matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, which silently swallowed public/data/dashboard.json -- the one
# file the published dashboard reads. CI would have committed nothing and
# deployed a page with no data, reporting success the whole way.
/data/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- dashboard build ---
node_modules/
dist/

# results/ is deliberately NOT ignored. §8 requires every result dir to carry
# its config and git hash, and §1's fourth objective is a DOCUMENTED "no edge
# found" outcome -- a null result that exists only on one disk is not
# documented. They are small text files; the plan doc carries the narrative and
# these carry the raw output it was written from.
